00:38:46.640 --> 00:38:48.481
So how do you balance the short

00:38:48.481 --> 00:38:50.544
term share price responsibility

00:38:50.544 --> 00:38:52.608
that you have versus the long term

00:38:52.608 --> 00:38:54.380
customer pain point view?

00:38:54.380 --> 00:38:56.510
&gt;&gt; That's a really good question.

00:38:56.510 --> 00:38:57.742
I think that one, yeah,

00:38:57.742 --> 00:38:58.974
this is another mentor,

00:38:58.974 --> 00:38:59.804
my mentor also.

00:38:59.804 --> 00:39:02.840
And I learn a lot from him as well.

00:39:04.230 --> 00:39:07.340
The company called Nvidia, right?

00:39:07.340 --> 00:39:09.710
And by the founder and CEO, Jason,

00:39:09.710 --> 00:39:11.850
also the Stanford alum as well.

00:39:11.850 --> 00:39:13.434
See, all the student alumni

00:39:13.434 --> 00:39:15.285
accomplishment very well, so.

00:39:15.285 --> 00:39:16.885
You look at Nvidia,

00:39:16.885 --> 00:39:18.990
the company history.

00:39:18.990 --> 00:39:20.803
I remember there's a time,

00:39:20.803 --> 00:39:22.012
ten years in a row,

00:39:22.012 --> 00:39:23.685
the stock price was flat.

00:39:23.685 --> 00:39:25.629
Look at it today, number one

00:39:25.629 --> 00:39:28.302
semiconductor company, because make

00:39:28.302 --> 00:39:30.570
sure as a leader, right, always

00:39:30.570 --> 00:39:32.940
focus on long term goal, right?

00:39:32.940 --> 00:39:34.466
Do not focus on short term, and

